--[[
The entry point.

Everything the command line is lives under `nupp.tools.cli`: one derived
command record per subcommand and the application that resolves and runs those
typed records. What is left here is the two things a program has to do that a
library cannot: read `arg`, and exit with a status.
]]

-- Windows opens the inherited standard streams in text mode. That changes LF
-- output to CRLF and, more seriously, changes the bytes and Content-Length of
-- an LSP frame after it was measured. CLI protocols and generated artifacts
-- are byte contracts, so put all three standard descriptors in binary mode.
if package.config:sub(1, 1) == "\\" then
    cdef function _setmode(descriptor: int32, mode: int32): int32
    const BINARY = 0x8000
    _setmode(0, BINARY)
    _setmode(1, BINARY)
    _setmode(2, BINARY)
end

-- Before anything else is required, because what it does is decide how the rest
-- of this compiler gets loaded. It is a cache and answers nothing when it has
-- nothing to answer with, so a checkout without one, or with a stale one, simply
-- loads the way it always did.
-- What the VM CLI's root sets up too: the trivia store the parser writes into,
-- and the loader that answers `load`, `loadstring` and `loadfile` with chunks
-- the VM lowers, which reading a manifest needs.
require("nupp.compiler.syntax.triviaarena").install(require("nupp.compiler.syntax.triviaarena.table"))
require("nupp.compiler.vm.chunks").install()

local code = require("nupp.tools.cli").main(arg)
os.exit(code)
